{comment: Verse 1 — the ones behind the desk}
[G]Before the first string rang [D]you were taping down the lines,
[Em]four tops aimed out from the [C]circle, a monitor at every knee.
[G]You rode the faders for a [D]tabla and a laptop and a child,
[Em]and you made the shy ones [C]loud enough to hear themselves be free.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Thank you, everyone who showed [G]up — the orchestra was you.
[D]No auditions and no gatekeepers, [G]no wrong instrument, no queue.
[C]You sat on the floor in [G]Mumbai and the floor became a hall,
[D]a sanctuary where the healing [G]was the music, that was all.

{comment: Verse 2 — the ones who danced}
[G]You didn't come to perform, [D]you came to move the room,
[Em]barefoot on the rugs with [C]the mandala on your back.
[G]Thirty-five of us took turns [D]at the mics across four days,
[Em]but the ones who danced were the [C]orchestra, and we never lost the track.

{comment: Verse 3 — the baby on the floor}
[G]There was a baby on the [D]floor and someone handed her the sticks,
[Em]and she found the drum [C]before she found the words.
[G]Her first beat landed late and [D]the whole circle landed with it —
[Em]that was the truest downbeat [C]that any of us heard.

{comment: Chorus}
(repeat)

{comment: Verse 4 — the one who sat in silence}
[G]And there was one who [D]carries the weight of Ethereum's name
[Em]who came in without a [C]speech and didn't take a chair.
[G]Just sat in the circle, [D]silent, with nothing to defend —
[Em]and if even you could feel safe [C]here, then everyone was safe in there.

{comment: Verse 5 — the singers, the saxes, the first-timers}
[G]Indian voices lifting [D]ragas, saxophones answering back,
[Em]DJs trading decks with live coders, [C]a ukulele learning its three chords.
[G]Someone played for the first time ever [D]and the room held them like water —
[Em]every voice a node, every sound [C]a contribution, and nobody kept score.

{comment: Bridge — the last evening}
[G]Friday the sixth, Dhanteras, [D]the first lamp of Diwali —
[Em]a brass lamp lit in the circle [C]where the drums had been all week.
[G]Then confetti under the mandala [D]and the whole of Devcon dancing,
[Em]and the Sanctuary held the closing [C]like it held the first one meek.

{comment: Last chorus}
[C]Thank you, everyone who showed [G]up — the orchestra was you.
[D]From the sound crew to the dancers [G]to the baby to the quiet one, too.
[C]We rest, we heal, we [G]play again — the circle isn't done —
[D]see you on the floor [G]in Lisbon. Every contribution is one. 🪷
